<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.6">
  <world name="mcity">

    <!-- ============================================================
         Mcity == a Gazebo Classic recreation of the University of
         Michigan's Mcity autonomous-vehicle test facility.

         PROVENANCE
           Source: osrf/car_demo (github.com/osrf/car_demo), the world
           OSRF built for their Prius/Gazebo self-driving demo (2017,
           ROS Kinetic + Gazebo 8/9). That repo is archived (EOL Feb
           2025), but the standalone "mcity" model == mesh, materials
           and its own model.sdf/model.config == loads fine on Gazebo
           Classic 11 with no dependency on the rest of it.
           Model author, per its own model.config: Nate Koenig, OSRF.

           NOTE ON LICENSING: no LICENSE file ships with that repo. It
           has been openly shared and reused across the ROS/Gazebo
           community for years, but that is not the same as a formal
           licence grant. Fine for internal research; check before it
           appears in anything published.

         ============================================================
         SCALE WAS HALVED ON 2026-08-21 == 0.254 to 0.127
         ============================================================
         The mesh scale in models/mcity/model.sdf was wrong by a factor
         of two, which made every kerb in town 0.316 m tall == 1.9x the
         Husky's 0.1651 m wheel radius, i.e. an impassable wall. At
         0.127 the kerb is 0.158 m, matching the US 6-inch standard and
         just under one wheel radius. The reasoning and the measurements
         are written up in models/mcity/model.sdf; read that before
         changing the number again.

         EVERY COORDINATE BELOW IS IN THE NEW SCALE. Sidewalk surfaces
         are now at z = 0.158 (were 0.316) and the town is 292 x 463 m
         (was 584 x 925). Any note or measurement from before that date
         quoting the old numbers is stale.

         ============================================================
         VERIFIED ON THIS INSTALL (measured, not assumed)
         ============================================================
         Every property that has previously broken a mapping run here
         was checked against the mesh before adopting this world:

         1. TEXTURES TILE, they do not stretch.  This is the one that
            matters most. The mesh is low-poly == 4153 vertices, 7333
            faces, so if its UVs ran 0..1 each face would smear a single
            copy of its texture over tens of metres and yield almost no
            features. They do not: the UV range is u -512..417,
            v -321..2039, i.e. the textures repeat many times per face
            and stay sharp. For contrast, an untextured world here
            measured 13 ORB keypoints in a 1920x1200 image against the
            20 RTAB-Map needs.

         2. IT HAS COLLISION GEOMETRY.  model.sdf declares the same
            mesh as both <collision> and <visual>, so the robot drives
            on it rather than falling through. There is deliberately
            no ground_plane in this world: the mesh already provides
            the ground, and a plane at z=0 would z-fight the roads.

         3. THE SURFACES ARE REAL.  16 materials, including separate
            Concrete_Ground (sidewalk), Curb, Crosswalk, Grass, Gravel,
            Asphalt and FIVE road variants == Road_Blank,
            Road_Blank_Light, Road_DoubleYellowLine,
            Road_DoubleYellowLine_Light and Road_SingleWhiteLine. The
            two "_Light" variants are easy to miss and cover most of the
            streets near the spawn; a search that omits them concludes
            there is no road nearby, which is wrong.

         4. IT IS FULLY OFFLINE.  All 22 textures ship with the model.
            Nothing is fetched from Fuel at load time.
         ============================================================ -->

    <include>
      <uri>model://sun</uri>
    </include>

    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>1000</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <include>
      <uri>model://mcity</uri>
    </include>


    <!-- ==================================================================
         PEDESTRIANS AND PARKED CARS
         added 2026-08-21, re-placed the same day after the rescale

         AUTHORED, NOT IMPORTED. Checked first: this Gazebo install ships
         no person, pedestrian or vehicle models, and no skeleton
         animations, and the project runs fully offline so Fuel is not an
         option. These are therefore built from primitives.

         They are STAND-INS, and honest about it: a box-and-sphere figure
         reads as a person at 5 m but will not fool anyone up close, and
         every surface is a building texture because those are the only
         textured materials available. What matters for SLAM is that they
         are vertical, feature-bearing and unevenly spaced == all three of
         which they are.

         They are STATIC. Gazebo <actor> can move a model along a
         trajectory, but without skeleton animation files a walking person
         would slide rather than walk. Dynamic pedestrians are Phase 7 work
         and want doing properly.

         THE SCENE THEY MAKE
           The robot spawns on the sidewalk at (-12.375, -56.140) facing
           -x, which puts the street on its LEFT and the walking line
           ahead of it. So it drives the sidewalk with parked cars passing
           on the left and pedestrians ahead == the actual situation a
           sidewalk robot has to handle, rather than props scattered for
           the sake of features.

         PLACEMENT IS PROBED, NOT GUESSED. Each (x, y) below was tested
         against the mesh by finding the face directly underneath it, so
         every prop stands on a surface that is really there and its z
         comes from that surface:

             people  ->  Concrete_Ground, z = 0.158  (the sidewalk)
             cars    ->  Road_DoubleYellowLine_Light, z = 0.000  (the road)

         This replaces the first attempt, where all eight were dropped on
         concrete because a road search that omitted the "_Light"
         materials reported no carriageway within 45 m. One car also
         landed over a hole in the mesh with no surface under it at all
         and hung in mid-air, since these models are static and do not
         fall. Probe the ground before adding anything else here.
    ================================================================== -->

    <!-- People: on the sidewalk, z 0.158. Legs 0.558, torso 1.258, head 1.658. -->

    <model name="person_1"><static>true</static><pose>-16.5 -56.14 0 0 0 1.9</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="legs"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Road</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="torso"><pose>0 0 1.258 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.44 0.28 0.60</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/PaintedWall</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="head"><pose>0 0 1.658 0 0 0</pose><geometry><sphere><radius>0.10</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/WoodPallet</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="person_2"><static>true</static><pose>-21.0 -56.14 0 0 0 -0.6</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="legs"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Motorway</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="torso"><pose>0 0 1.258 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.44 0.28 0.60</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Residential</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="head"><pose>0 0 1.658 0 0 0</pose><geometry><sphere><radius>0.10</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/WoodPallet</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="person_3"><static>true</static><pose>-26.0 -56.14 0 0 0 2.7</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="legs"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Steps</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="torso"><pose>0 0 1.258 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.44 0.28 0.60</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Bricks</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="head"><pose>0 0 1.658 0 0 0</pose><geometry><sphere><radius>0.10</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/WoodPallet</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="person_4"><static>true</static><pose>-19.0 -54.12 0 0 0 0.4</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="legs"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Road</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="torso"><pose>0 0 1.258 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.44 0.28 0.60</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Steps</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="head"><pose>0 0 1.658 0 0 0</pose><geometry><sphere><radius>0.10</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/WoodPallet</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="person_5"><static>true</static><pose>-30.0 -56.14 0 0 0 1.2</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="legs"><pose>0 0 0.558 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.34 0.26 0.80</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Motorway</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="torso"><pose>0 0 1.258 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>0.44 0.28 0.60</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Wood</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="head"><pose>0 0 1.658 0 0 0</pose><geometry><sphere><radius>0.10</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/WoodPallet</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <!-- Cars: on the carriageway, z 0.000. Body 0.375, cabin 1.075.
         Yaw is set along the street (near 0 or near pi) so they read as
         traffic rather than as boxes dropped at an angle. -->

    <model name="car_1"><static>true</static><pose>-16.0 -60.40 0 0 0 0.02</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="body"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/PioneerBody</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="cabin"><pose>-0.25 0 1.075 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2.2 1.65 0.65</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="car_2"><static>true</static><pose>-22.5 -62.40 0 0 0 3.13</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="body"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Motorway</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="cabin"><pose>-0.25 0 1.075 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2.2 1.65 0.65</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <model name="car_3"><static>true</static><pose>-28.0 -60.40 0 0 0 0.05</pose>
      <link name="l">
        <collision name="c"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="body"><pose>0 0 0.375 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>4.4 1.8 0.75</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/Road</name></script></material></visual>
        <visual name="cabin"><pose>-0.25 0 1.075 0 0 0</pose><geometry><box><size>2.2 1.65 0.65</size></box></geometry>
          <material><script><uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri><name>Gazebo/CeilingTiled</name></script></material></visual>
      </link></model>

    <scene>
      <ambient>0.55 0.55 0.55 1</ambient>
      <background>0.72 0.77 0.83 1</background>
      <shadows>false</shadows>
    </scene>

    <!-- Initial viewer camera, declared here rather than pushed at runtime
         over /gazebo/<world>/user_camera/pose == that route repeatedly left
         the viewport black and leaked hung `gz topic` processes. Placed to
         look up the street at the spawn, so the robot, the pedestrians on
         the sidewalk and the parked cars on the road are all in the opening
         frame without anyone having to hunt for them. -->
    <gui>
      <camera name="user_camera">
        <pose>-26.4 -72.1 14 0 0.582 0.852</pose>
      </camera>
    </gui>

  </world>
</sdf>
